+# Outbound webhooks
+
+Customers register an HTTPS endpoint and we POST every subscribed event to it.
+
+## Registering an endpoint
+
+```
+POST /v1/settings/webhook-endpoints
+{"url": "https://hooks.example.com/acme", "event_types": ["invoice.paid"]}
+```
+
+Only `https://` URLs are accepted. An empty `event_types` subscribes the
+endpoint to every event type we emit. The response is the only place the
+signing secret appears — it cannot be read back afterwards, so store it in your
+own secret manager.
+
+## Verifying the signature
+
+Every request carries `X-Acme-Timestamp` (unix seconds at signing time) and
+`X-Acme-Signature` (`sha256=<hex>`). The signature is the HMAC-SHA256 of
+`"{timestamp}.{raw_request_body}"` keyed with your signing secret. Compare it
+against your own computation using a constant-time comparison, and reject
+requests whose timestamp is more than five minutes old — that window is what
+stops a captured request from being replayed.
+
+## Retries
+
+- a delivery is attempted at most 5 times
+- backoff is exponential with jitter, roughly 2s, 4s, 8s, 16s
+- any 2xx marks the delivery `delivered`; 5xx, timeouts and connection errors
+  are retried; a 4xx is permanent and we stop immediately
+- delivery is at-least-once, so deduplicate on `event_id`
+
+## Inspecting deliveries
+
+`GET /v1/settings/webhook-endpoints/{id}/deliveries` returns the most recent
+attempts for an endpoint belonging to your organization, including the response
+status we saw and when the next attempt is scheduled.
